# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 72-74 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 10 — CHAPTER 12, 2026-09-20; the one run): "you may not eat within your gates" (72), the
# headless 73 (12:17's herd and flock) and 74 (12:17's vows; 12:18-19) — EVERY ROW READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch12_ink.SP_; the middah where the
# row argues by one (checked). Chapter 11's form.
from ch12_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(72, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU MAY NOT EAT WITHIN YOUR GATES" (12:17) — R. JOSHUA BEN KORHAH: I AM ABLE, BUT I AM NOT PERMITTED. LIKEWISE "THE JEBUSITES … THE SONS OF JUDAH COULD NOT DISPOSSESS" (JOSHUA 15:63) — THEY COULD, BUT WERE NOT PERMITTED. "NOT ABLE" READ AS "NOT PERMITTED" — the head row of piska 72 ({SP_(72, 1, "יכול", "אני", "אבל", "איני", "רשי")} "I am able, but I am not permitted"): THE INK: "you may not" eight in the book (computed); Onkelos the same reading ("you have no permission", the ink); THE RUN: Joshua 15:63 read as the same idiom — the Jebusites left by permission, not by weakness. Fresh.')
srow(72, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE TITHE" — ONLY IN CLEANNESS? IN UNCLEANNESS WHENCE? "YOUR GRAIN." ({SP_(72, 2, "טמא", "מנין")} "the unclean whence"): the second tithe eaten within the wall in cleanness — the translator\'s note on the elliptic syntax (the English); Makkot 19b at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(72, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'BOUGHT WITH TITHE MONEY WHENCE? "YOUR WINE." ({SP_(72, 3, "לקוח", "בכסף", "מעשר", "מנין")} "bought with tithe money whence"): 14:24-26 (ahead). Fresh.')
srow(72, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'ONLY IN CLEANNESS? IN UNCLEANNESS WHENCE? "YOUR OIL." ({SP_(72, 4, "תלמוד", "לומר", "ויצהרך")} "the Teaching states: your oil"): the three nouns three inclusions. Fresh.')
srow(72, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON: FROM "I HAVE NOT EATEN OF IT IN MY MOURNING NOR REMOVED OF IT WHILE UNCLEAN" (26:14) — WHERE IS HE WARNED? I DO NOT KNOW: "YOU MAY NOT EAT WITHIN YOUR GATES THE TITHE." THE WARNING FOUND ({SP_(72, 5, "היכן", "הוא", "מזהר", "איני", "יודע")} "where is he warned I do not know"): 26:14\'s confession presupposes a prohibition — 12:17 supplies it (the shelf\'s rule: no punishment without a warning); Makkot 19b at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(72, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT ONE WHO GIVES IT AS A GIFT BE LIABLE? "YOU MAY NOT EAT" — THE EATER IS LIABLE, NOT THE GIVER. ({SP_(72, 6, "האוכל", "חיב", "ואין", "הנותן", "במתנה", "חיב")} "the eater is liable, and not the giver"): the verb\'s object a PARAMETER of the liable party. Fresh.')
srow(72, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: MIGHT THEY BE LIABLE ONLY FOR UNTITHED PRODUCE FROM WHICH NOTHING WAS TAKEN? WHENCE IF THE HEAVE OFFERING WAS TAKEN BUT NOT THE FIRST TITHE, THE FIRST BUT NOT THE SECOND, EVEN NOT THE POOR TITHE? "YOU MAY NOT EAT WITHIN YOUR GATES." ({SP_(72, 7, "הורם", "ממנו", "תרומה", "ולא", "הורם", "ממנו", "מעשר", "ראשון")} "the heave offering taken from it and not the first tithe"): the tithes\' ORDER a PARAMETER (heave, first, second, poor — Tosefta Makkot 4:4, the English); Makkot 16b-17a at 10b. Fresh.')
srow(72, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON: THE VERSE COMES ONLY TO SET A PARTITION BETWEEN HOLY THINGS AND HOLY THINGS. ({SP_(72, 8, "לתן", "מחצה", "בין", "קדשים", "לקדשים")} "to set a partition between holy things and holy things"); no citation in either file — 71:12\'s counter. Fresh.')
srow(72, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE HEAVE OFFERING OF YOUR HAND" — THE FIRST FRUITS. WHAT DOES THE VERSE TEACH? IF THAT ONE WHO EATS FIRST FRUITS OUTSIDE THE WALL TRANSGRESSES — A FORTIORI FROM THE TITHE: THE TITHE, PERMITTED TO NON-PRIESTS, ITS EATER OUTSIDE THE WALL TRANSGRESSES; FIRST FRUITS, FORBIDDEN TO NON-PRIESTS, ALL THE MORE. RATHER: ONE WHO EATS FIRST FRUITS BEFORE THE DECLARATION TRANSGRESSES. ({SP_(72, 9, "לאוכל", "בכורים", "עד", "שלא", "קרא", "עליהם")} "one who eats first fruits before he has read over them"): I1 (checked) — the a fortiori shows the plain reading redundant, so the verse is assigned a new case (Mishnah Makkot 3:3 — the English); THE FORM OF PISKAOT 72-74: each item of 12:17\'s list assigned by elimination through a ladder of a fortiori arguments — 72:9, 72:10, 72:11, 73:1, 74:1 one method five times; no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(72, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOUR FREEWILL OFFERINGS" — THE THANK OFFERING AND THE PEACE OFFERING. IF OUTSIDE THE WALL — A FORTIORI FROM THE TITHE (NOT LIABLE FOR PIGGUL, LEFTOVER OR UNCLEANNESS, YET ITS EATER OUTSIDE TRANSGRESSES); RATHER: ONE WHO EATS THEM BEFORE THE BLOOD IS THROWN TRANSGRESSES. ({SP_(72, 10, "לאוכל", "תודה", "ושלמים", "לפני", "זריקת", "דמים")} "one who eats the thank and peace offerings before the throwing of the blood"): I1 (checked) — the ladder\'s second rung; the translator\'s notes on piggul and leftover (the English). Fresh.')
srow(72, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE FIRSTLINGS" — THE FIRSTBORN. IF OUTSIDE THE WALL — FROM THE TITHE; IF BEFORE THE THROWING — FROM THE THANK AND PEACE OFFERINGS (PERMITTED TO NON-PRIESTS, YET BEFORE THE THROWING FORBIDDEN; THE FIRSTBORN, FORBIDDEN TO NON-PRIESTS, ALL THE MORE). RATHER: A NON-PRIEST WHO EATS THE FIRSTBORN\'S FLESH, BEFORE OR AFTER THE THROWING, TRANSGRESSES. ({SP_(72, 11, "לזר", "שאכל", "בשר", "בכור")} "a non-priest who ate the flesh of a firstborn"): I1 (checked) twice — the third rung; the firstborn the priest\'s (Numbers 18:17-18, read). Fresh.')

srow(73, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"OF YOUR HERD AND YOUR FLOCK" (12:17) — THE SIN AND GUILT OFFERINGS. IF OUTSIDE THE WALL — FROM THE TITHE; BEFORE THE THROWING — FROM THE THANK AND PEACE OFFERINGS; AFTER THE THROWING — FROM THE FIRSTBORN (LESSER HOLY, YET ITS EATER AFTER THE THROWING TRANSGRESSES; SIN AND GUILT, MOST HOLY, ALL THE MORE). RATHER: ONE WHO EATS A SIN OR GUILT OFFERING OUTSIDE THE CURTAINS TRANSGRESSES. THE HEADLESS PISKA 73 — its one row opening with 12:17\'s own words ({SP_(73, 1, "לאוכל", "חטאת", "ואשם", "חוץ", "לקלעים")} "one who eats a sin or guilt offering outside the curtains"): I1 (checked) three rungs — the fourth item; "outside the curtains" the Tabernacle\'s boundary (Leviticus 6:9, 7:6 — the English\'s note): the court a PARAMETER of the most holy\'s eating. Fresh.')

srow(74, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOUR VOWS" (12:17) — THE BURNT OFFERING. OUTSIDE THE WALL — FROM THE TITHE; BEFORE THE THROWING — FROM THE THANK AND PEACE; AFTER — FROM THE FIRSTBORN; OUTSIDE THE CURTAINS — FROM THE SIN AND GUILT (PERMITTED TO EAT, YET OUTSIDE THE CURTAINS FORBIDDEN; THE BURNT OFFERING, FORBIDDEN TO EAT, ALL THE MORE). RATHER: ONE WHO EATS A BURNT OFFERING, BEFORE OR AFTER THE THROWING, INSIDE OR OUTSIDE THE CURTAINS, TRANSGRESSES. THE HEADLESS PISKA 74 — its first row 12:17\'s "your vows" ({SP_(74, 1, "נדריך", "זו", "עולה")} "your vows — this is the burnt offering"; {SP_(74, 1, "בין", "לפנים", "מן", "הקלעים", "בין", "חוץ", "לקלעים")} "whether inside the curtains or outside the curtains"): I1 (checked) four rungs — the fifth item, the ladder\'s top: the burnt offering never eaten; the list of 12:17 a decision table of five prohibitions (the compile\'s cells). Fresh.')
srow(74, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"BUT BEFORE THE LORD YOUR GOD" (12:18) — THIS IS SHILOH. ({SP_(74, 2, "זו", "שילה")} "this is Shiloh"): 12:18\'s two clauses read as two stations again (62:3, 68:6). Fresh.')
srow(74, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU SHALL EAT IT IN THE PLACE WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD WILL CHOOSE" — THIS IS JERUSALEM. ({SP_(74, 3, "זו", "ירושלם")} "this is Jerusalem"). Fresh.')
srow(74, 4, 'CONTEXT', f'"YOU, YOUR SON, YOUR DAUGHTER, YOUR MANSERVANT AND YOUR MAIDSERVANT" — THE DEARER FIRST (69:3 again, on the singular list — THE INK: 5:14\'s Sabbath household, computed). ({SP_(74, 4, "חביב", "חביב", "קודם")} "the dearer first"). Fresh.')
srow(74, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THE LEVITE WITHIN YOUR GATES" — GIVE HIM OF HIS PORTION; THE POOR TITHE; PEACE OFFERINGS (69:4 again). ({SP_(74, 5, "תן", "לו", "שלמים")} "give him peace offerings"). Fresh.')
srow(74, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'"TAKE HEED" (12:19) — A PROHIBITION. ({SP_(74, 6, "השמר", "בלא", "תעשה")} "take heed — a prohibition"): 70:1 again. Fresh.')
srow(74, 7, 'CONTEXT', f'"LEST" — A PROHIBITION. ({SP_(74, 7, "פן", "בלא", "תעשה")} "lest — a prohibition"). Fresh.')
srow(74, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"LEST YOU FORSAKE THE LEVITE ALL YOUR DAYS" — EVEN IN SABBATICAL YEARS AND JUBILEES. ({SP_(74, 8, "אפלו", "שמטים", "ואפלו", "יובלות")} "even sabbaticals and even jubilees"): "all your days" a PARAMETER of time without exception — the years without tithes still bind; THE INK: the Levite\'s verse shares two tokens with no verse of the Bible (computed). Fresh.')
srow(74, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"ON YOUR LAND" — AND NOT IN THE EXILE. ({SP_(74, 9, "ולא", "בגולה")} "and not in the exile"): the duty\'s place a PARAMETER — the Land (59:5\'s rule applied). Fresh.')

assert sorted(S) == [(72, r) for r in range(1, 12)] + [(73, 1)] + [(74, r) for r in range(1, 10)], sorted(S)
